Approach: Split the string into words, reverse the word array using recursion, then join the words back with spaces and trim extra spaces.

Time Complexity: O(n) — splitting, reversing, and joining together take linear time.

Space Complexity: O(n) — extra space used for storing split words.

class Solution {
    public String reverseWords(String s) {
        String arr[]=s.split("\\s+");
        int i=0,j=arr.length-1;
        arr=reverse(arr,i,j);
        return String.join(" ",arr).trim();
